# rmscgate_rpmnew.yaml.rpmnew - the silent exception to the filename rule.
#
# EXERCISES  the one filename that fails the regex and is ignored WITHOUT a
#            warning. This is a real situation, not a contrivance: `yum update`
#            drops .rpmnew beside a service definition it did not overwrite, and
#            a warning for every one of them on every command would be noise.
# UPSTREAM   ignored, silently. No service, no warning, on either stream.
# RMSC       identical.
# BASIS      measured - 'a name that does not match is ignored with a warning,
#            except one ending rpmnew which is ignored silently'.
# STAGING    none.
# ISOLATION  no - and that is the point. It is the only rejected-filename case
#            that can live in the main pack, because it is the only one that adds
#            no output. If it ever starts warning, every other comparison in the
#            pack picks up an extra line and the perturbation shows up as a
#            wholesale failure rather than as one row.
# FAILS IF   a service named rmscgate_rpmnew (or rmscgate_rpmnew.yaml) appears in
#            `list`, or any line on either stream mentions this filename.
# NOTE       This fixture asserts an ABSENCE, so it cannot prove it was ever
#            installed. Install it together with rmscgate_badname (isolation),
#            whose warning proves the same directory is being scanned - or check
#            that the file arrived.
name: RMSC gate rpmnew
start_cmd: /QOpenSys/usr/bin/true
check_alive: 55456
